  "assessments": [
    {
      "section": "16.1 motivation",
      "judgment": "14.3 owned release receiver and pending recv borrow give a concrete internal-reference motivation, expressly not guaranteed compiler struct layout. Not every future is claimed self-referential. Lifetime, ownership transfer and physical location are distinguished; self pointers are not automatically repaired."
    },
    {
      "section": "16.1 source/outputs",
      "judgment": "Reference version keeps field borrows live through swap, supporting E0502. AddressNote stores i32/raw pointer and only ptr::eq, never dereferences invalid saved; construction occurs before remember. Whole-value swap moves saved with values and produces false/false, including equal values; Box-owner swap leaves allocations and true/true; field-only swap preserves field addresses/records. Four tests, answers and exact output agree; shared module copies match."
    },
    {
      "section": "16.2 Pin contract",
      "judgment": "Pin wrapper versus pointee, mutable borrowed versus owned forms, library/unsafe contract, Unpin opt-out and PhantomPinned are accurate. Pin::new/get_mut Unpin conditions and rejection E0277 are correct; Box::pin does not require Unpin. Pin as_ref/as_mut/get_ref/get_unchecked_mut receiver ownership/bounds are introduced before use. BoxPin owner movement does not move pointee, ordinaryBox lacks protection, and !Unpin is not permanent no-move from construction."
    },
    {
      "section": "16.2 model and Drop",
      "judgment": "PinnedNote fields private; constructor first Box::pin then records location. Both unsafe mutable getters modify only intended i32/raw field, do not replace/move Self, leak mutable reference or offer structural pin projection. Drop only reads i32/compares raw address; Drop receiver stays&mut and Drop guarantee includes storage reclamation/reuse, not guaranteed eventual cleanup. Seven-line owner-swap/drop sequence and solution100 are accurate. Local pin! creates local borrowed Pin without T heap allocation; async storage caveat avoids equatinglocal withstack. Reborrow tests preserve same pointee and correctly use as_mut repeatedly."
    },
    {
      "section": "closure/figures",
      "judgment": "Stages package truly has no library or dependencies; nine selected run/test commands load only listed target-local modules. Complete target includes all seven stated tests and taught helpers, no future poll/runtime source. Three standalone failure files fully inline with sidecars; no subsequent lib needed. Three SVG XML labels/arrows match the address model and explicitly distinguish sequence/address/ownership, not measured layout or dereference permission."
    }
